          "en": "from a different origin?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 42.03,
          "end": 43.29,
          "en": "And that's a risky part, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 43.29,
          "end": 45.03,
          "en": "So that's not security.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 45.03,
          "end": 46.65,
          "en": "So if you want to make it more secure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 46.65,
          "end": 47.79,
          "en": "by default, Spring says,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 47.79,
          "end": 50.67,
          "en": "hey, you're not allowed to directly access a resource",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 50.67,
          "end": 52.17,
          "en": "from the outside origin.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 52.17,
          "end": 53.61,
          "en": "And if you want to allow it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 53.61,
          "end": 55.5,
          "en": "of course we have to allow it in our application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 55.5,
          "end": 57.51,
          "en": "because we are running on two different ports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 57.51,
          "end": 58.95,
          "en": "or two different origins.",
